    "scope": "A canonical ZIP_STORED codec admits safe regular entries with exact inventory and external byte identity. The package_kind=work transport retains every reachable generation, inventory segment, manifest and semantic object. All container, build, schema, original and successor bindings are checked before target publication. The target must be missing or private and empty under the native Work mutex; existing stores, symlinks and protected overlaps are refused. Restore republishes original generations through the durable native store, creates a fresh root-inode binding and preserves actual successful prefixes on I/O failure. Native write work is explicitly unsupported rather than exported with unknown Recovery state. Initial read-only host APIs and whole-byte ZIP32 processing only. Full Work CLI, general executable workflows, normative work export with current transaction/receipt proof and explicit write-target mapping, incremental large export and multipart archives remain open. No native Recovery substitute, executable code loading, authenticity from internal self-consistency, semantic success from generic data, or release approval is claimed."
